  "notes": "Governmental funds cash basis (Total column p4); business-type Water/Sewer fund accrual basis (p6, measure net position). Transfers: governmental Total column prints net transfers out (152,193) to Water/Sewer (General out 333,276; other governmental funds in 181,083); pass-through grant in/out 71,511 nets to zero in other_financing. Water/Sewer 'Debt payment' 65,000 and interest 25,701 are printed as other expense on p6 and recorded as business-type disbursements as printed. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Financial Position, Total - Memorandum Only column (p1), kept because it holds capital assets and debt; its 'Total liabilities' 1,290,000 covers only long-term liabilities, so total_liabilities is taken from p5 (1,423,101). Detail: the only governmental supplementary schedule is the combined all-governmental-funds budget schedule (p9), so per user rule detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4) and the combined schedule lines are not recorded; Water/Sewer uses its own cash-basis budget schedule (p10, budget and actual) rather than the accrual statement lines. Proprietary cash flow statement (p7) left out (proprietary null for cash-basis reports): operating -45,517, capital and related financing 61,492, noncapital 25,738, cash 126,008 to 167,721. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
